            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An exemplary bursting capsule includes a hollow cavity completely enclosed and delimited by a vessel wall comprising a frangible material, a rupturing fluid disposed in the hollow cavity, an electrical conductor disposed on an outside surface of the vessel wall, and a conformal coating on at least a portion of the outside surface covering the electrical conductor.</p>
